---
import DesignLayout from '../layouts/DesignLayout.astro';
---
<DesignLayout
  section="07 / Data graphics"
  title="Show the comparison people already know how to read."
  focus="Which conventional chart makes the decision, change or trade-off clearest?"
  description="GreenSquare AI standards for traditional business charts, graphs and think-cell-style decision graphics."
>
  <section class="v3-section chart-principles">
    <div class="v3-split">
      <div>
        <span class="identity-kicker">Traditional first</span>
        <h2 class="v3-section-title-sm">The chart is evidence, not decoration.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="v3-lede">Use columns, bars, lines and waterfalls before specialist decision graphics. Familiar forms reduce interpretation time.</p>
        <ol class="chart-rule-list">
          <li><strong>Lead with the conclusion.</strong><span>Use a sentence title, not a topic label.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Label the data directly.</strong><span>Remove legends where the series can be named at the line or bar.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Use colour to make one distinction.</strong><span>Context stays neutral; the material series or variance carries colour.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Show the comparison.</strong><span>Add targets, deltas, CAGR, confidence ranges or decision thresholds only when they change the reading.</span></li>
          <li><strong>State source and basis.</strong><span>Unit, period, scope, source and assumptions belong with the chart.</span></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v3-section chart-gallery" aria-label="Approved chart examples">
    <figure class="chart-specimen chart-specimen--wide">
      <figcaption><span>01 / Clustered column</span><strong>Partner model closes the annual cost gap by FY27</strong><p>Use for direct comparison across a small number of categories or periods.</p></figcaption>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 900 400" role="img" aria-label="Clustered column chart comparing current and partner model costs from FY25 to FY28">
        <line class="chart-axis" x1="70" y1="330" x2="840" y2="330" />
        <line class="chart-target" x1="70" y1="135" x2="840" y2="135" />
        <text class="chart-annotation" x="735" y="122">Break-even threshold €12.0m</text>
        <g class="chart-pair"><rect class="chart-context" x="120" y="75" width="54" height="255"/><rect class="chart-highlight" x="178" y="94" width="54" height="236"/><text x="147" y="62">15.8</text><text x="205" y="82">14.7</text><text x="176" y="356">FY25</text></g>
        <g class="chart-pair"><rect class="chart-context" x="305" y="91" width="54" height="239"/><rect class="chart-highlight" x="363" y="128" width="54" height="202"/><text x="332" y="78">14.9</text><text x="390" y="115">12.6</text><text x="361" y="356">FY26</text></g>
        <g class="chart-pair"><rect class="chart-context" x="490" y="109" width="54" height="221"/><rect class="chart-highlight" x="548" y="151" width="54" height="179"/><text x="517" y="96">13.8</text><text x="575" y="138">11.2</text><text x="546" y="356">FY27</text></g>
        <g class="chart-pair"><rect class="chart-context" x="675" y="126" width="54" height="204"/><rect class="chart-highlight" x="733" y="167" width="54" height="163"/><text x="702" y="113">12.7</text><text x="760" y="154">10.2</text><text x="731" y="356">FY28</text></g>
        <text class="chart-series" x="615" y="386">■ Current model</text><text class="chart-series chart-series--green" x="738" y="386">■ Partner model</text>
      </svg>
      <p class="chart-source">€m annual operating cost · FY25–FY28 planning case · Source: finance model v6 · Illustrative</p>
    </figure>

    <div class="chart-gallery-pair">
      <figure class="chart-specimen">
        <figcaption><span>02 / Line</span><strong>Churn converges only in the base case</strong><p>Use for movement over time. Label the series at its end.</p></figcaption>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 620 360" role="img" aria-label="Line chart showing base, downside and threshold churn rates">
          <line class="chart-axis" x1="62" y1="300" x2="560" y2="300" />
          <line class="chart-threshold" x1="62" y1="150" x2="560" y2="150" />
          <text class="chart-annotation" x="66" y="138">8% reversal threshold</text>
          <polyline class="chart-line chart-line--context" points="70,80 180,105 290,128 400,145 505,160" />
          <polyline class="chart-line chart-line--active" points="70,80 180,118 290,168 400,210 505,242" />
          <text x="515" y="164">Downside 7.4%</text><text class="chart-green-text" x="515" y="247">Base 4.1%</text>
          <text x="62" y="326">Q4</text><text x="172" y="326">Q1</text><text x="282" y="326">Q2</text><text x="392" y="326">Q3</text><text x="497" y="326">Q4</text>
        </svg>
        <p class="chart-source">Transferred-account churn · 12-month cohort · Source: partner diligence · Illustrative</p>
      </figure>

      <figure class="chart-specimen">
        <figcaption><span>03 / Waterfall</span><strong>Partner savings are partly offset by transition cost</strong><p>Use to explain how a starting value becomes an ending value.</p></figcaption>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 620 360" role="img" aria-label="Waterfall chart showing current cost, partner saving, transition and retained team costs">
          <line class="chart-axis" x1="55" y1="300" x2="575" y2="300" />
          <rect class="chart-total" x="68" y="74" width="72" height="226"/><text x="104" y="62">15.8</text>
          <line class="chart-connector" x1="140" y1="74" x2="184" y2="74"/><rect class="chart-positive" x="184" y="74" width="72" height="95"/><text x="220" y="62">−3.4</text>
          <line class="chart-connector" x1="256" y1="169" x2="300" y2="169"/><rect class="chart-negative" x="300" y="147" width="72" height="22"/><text x="336" y="136">+0.8</text>
          <line class="chart-connector" x1="372" y1="147" x2="416" y2="147"/><rect class="chart-negative" x="416" y="119" width="72" height="28"/><text x="452" y="108">+1.0</text>
          <rect class="chart-total chart-total--active" x="520" y="119" width="72" height="181"/><text x="556" y="108">14.2</text>
          <text x="104" y="326">Current</text><text x="220" y="326">Partner</text><text x="336" y="326">Transition</text><text x="452" y="326">Retained</text><text x="556" y="326">Future</text>
        </svg>
        <p class="chart-source">€m annualised cost · steady state plus year-one transition · Illustrative</p>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <figure class="chart-specimen chart-specimen--wide">
      <figcaption><span>04 / Stacked bar</span><strong>Strategic accounts concentrate revenue in every region</strong><p>Use stacked bars when composition matters; use 100% stacks only when share matters more than scale.</p></figcaption>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 900 360" role="img" aria-label="Stacked horizontal bars showing strategic and transferred account revenue by region">
        <text x="44" y="91">UK</text><rect class="chart-highlight" x="120" y="64" width="425" height="40"/><rect class="chart-context-light" x="545" y="64" width="218" height="40"/><text class="chart-inside" x="510" y="90">€8.5m</text><text x="776" y="90">€4.4m</text>
        <text x="44" y="166">EU</text><rect class="chart-highlight" x="120" y="139" width="335" height="40"/><rect class="chart-context-light" x="455" y="139" width="275" height="40"/><text class="chart-inside" x="420" y="165">€6.7m</text><text x="743" y="165">€5.5m</text>
        <text x="44" y="241">APAC</text><rect class="chart-highlight" x="120" y="214" width="230" height="40"/><rect class="chart-context-light" x="350" y="214" width="175" height="40"/><text class="chart-inside" x="315" y="240">€4.6m</text><text x="538" y="240">€3.5m</text>
        <text class="chart-series chart-series--green" x="120" y="305">■ Strategic / retained</text><text class="chart-series" x="310" y="305">■ Transfer candidate</text>
      </svg>
      <p class="chart-source">FY26 revenue by account treatment · Source: account portfolio · Illustrative</p>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="v3-section chart-selection">
    <div class="identity-section-head">
      <div><span class="identity-kicker">Selection rule</span><h2 class="v3-section-title-sm">Choose from the question.</h2></div>
      <p>Specialist formats are allowed when the decision genuinely requires them. Familiarity is a design advantage, not a constraint.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-choice-table" role="table" aria-label="Chart selection guide">
      <div class="chart-choice-row chart-choice-row--head"><span>Question</span><span>Use</span><span>Avoid when</span></div>
      <div class="chart-choice-row"><strong>How do categories compare?</strong><span>Bar or clustered column</span><span>There are more than 8–10 categories without a clear sort.</span></div>
      <div class="chart-choice-row"><strong>How did it change over time?</strong><span>Line or column</span><span>The periods are irregular or the line implies false continuity.</span></div>
      <div class="chart-choice-row"><strong>What drove the movement?</strong><span>Waterfall / bridge</span><span>The components do not reconcile to the total.</span></div>
      <div class="chart-choice-row"><strong>What is the composition?</strong><span>Stacked bar or Mekko</span><span>Precise segment comparison matters more than mix.</span></div>
      <div class="chart-choice-row"><strong>What is the relationship?</strong><span>Scatter or bubble</span><span>The sample is too small or causality is being implied.</span></div>
      <div class="chart-choice-row"><strong>When will work happen?</strong><span>Gantt</span><span>Dates, dependencies or owners are not maintained.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</DesignLayout>
